# Naming vocabulary (Teensy looper)

Use with global **`naming-and-terminology`**: clear **action + scope** (ideal two words; longer when needed for completeness), no abbreviations, reuse terms below.

Read before M8+ edit storage, OpenSpec **`m8-rename`** then **`m8-edit`**, or timeline refactors.

## Scope words (Loop slot)

| Scope | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Loop** | Slot container |
| **Capture** | Live record/overdub buffer (was `CaptureLayer`) |
| **Take** | Committed capture — Record or Overdub (was `Epoch`) |
| **Edit** | One committed `saveEdit` unit in `edits[]` |
| **EditChange** | One atomic change inside an **Edit** |
| **span** | Sub-period inside **NoteEditSession** (overdub boundary) |

## Types and ids

| Name | Role |
|------|------|
| **EditChangeType** | Enum of change types |
| **TakeType** | Record \| Overdub (was `EpochKind`) |
| **EditId** | Stable id per **Edit** |
| **NoteRef** | Stable note target in an **EditChange** |

## Edit sessions (RAM scope)

| Scope | UI domain |
|------|--------|
| **NoteEditSession** | Note edit (`EditManager`) — M8 |
| **LoopEditSession** | Loop length edit — future |
| **ControlChangeEditSession** | CC edit UI — future |
| **JamSession** / **PerformanceSession** | Playback/jam UI — **TBD** |

## Action + scope examples

| Name | Action | Scope |
|------|--------|-------|
| `commitTake()` | commit | Take |
| `saveEdit()` | save | Edit |
| `closeNoteEditSpan()` | close | NoteEditSpan |
| `applyEdits()` | apply | Edits |
| **TakeCommitted** | committed | Take (undo entry) |
| **NoteEditSessionCommitted** | committed | NoteEditSession (undo entry) |

## UI rename

- `class EditState` → **`EditNoteState`** (note-edit FSM base)
- **`EditState`** on struct **Edit** = Active \| Disabled (parallel **TakeState**)

## Words to avoid for new names

**segment**, **gesture**, **working**, **EditOp**, **published** (use **committed**), storing edits as Takes, new abbreviations. Prefer **Type** over **Kind** for new enums when the repo uses **Type** elsewhere.

Ask before introducing a **new domain noun** or session type name not listed above.
